# HavenWorld — Cline rules
# Source of truth: AGENTS.md in this repo root. Read it before starting any task.
# The non-negotiables below apply even if you read nothing else.

- Canonical gate: `make ci-docker` (5 steps). Gates run SOLO — check for
  running builds/gates first and wait for them to finish. Save the full gate
  output to a log file and report totals from the log, never from memory.
- Never skip the gate (no PUSH_CI_SKIP), and never skip, gate, or weaken a
  test to force a green run. Report failures exactly as they are.
- Every task is typed: [Goal], [Problem], or [Feature], with an objective and
  done criteria. Problems need red/green proof plus a regression test.
  Features must be verified live in the real UI (real clicks).
- Branch per task (`feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/` + slug). Open the PR on the
  first commit; update the same PR afterwards. NEVER merge a PR — merges are
  Daniel's only.
- A failure or out-of-scope problem becomes a GitHub issue: one per distinct
  failure signature, search open issues first, evidence + log excerpt
  required. Lint warnings roll into the standing tech-debt issue only.
- No secrets anywhere in code, issues, PRs, or chat. No deploys without
  Daniel's explicit go.
- Free models only (Free tab; "Input: Free / Output: Free"). Never click
  Add Credits or enable usage-based billing.
- Git: always `git --no-pager`, bounded output, bounded-timeout pushes.
- Verify from files, logs, and the live product — never from summaries,
  including your own. Re-read anything you claim to have written.
